64
00:06:05,879 --> 00:06:06,639
every week.

65
00:06:06,959 --> 00:06:08,240
Were you just in it for the food?

66
00:06:08,319 --> 00:06:09,040
Of course.

67
00:06:09,839 --> 00:06:11,120
What we're having here

68
00:06:11,199 --> 00:06:12,000
is youth.

69
00:06:12,959 --> 00:06:14,319
You've really changed a lot,

70
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:14,959
Ruan Sixian.

71
00:06:17,279 --> 00:06:17,800
Is there

72
00:06:18,199 --> 00:06:18,839
a Captain Yue

73
00:06:18,839 --> 00:06:19,600
at your airline?

74
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:20,800
You mean Yue Yang?

75
00:06:23,199 --> 00:06:25,319
He's kind of my instructor.

76
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:27,360
He came to our school

77
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,279
for a presentation last time

78
00:06:28,319 --> 00:06:29,319
and specifically praised you.

79
00:06:29,439 --> 00:06:30,560
He said you're improving fast

80
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:31,720
and really adaptable.

81
00:06:32,319 --> 00:06:33,040
It's nothing.

82
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:34,920
I just

83
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:36,800
want to do well with everything

84
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:37,800
I set out to do.

85
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:39,240
Also, I saw the whole

86
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:40,000
Hengshi Mayday incident

87
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:41,680
on the news.

88
00:06:41,839 --> 00:06:43,079
The captain passed out.

89
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:43,680
And

90
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:45,040
that terrible thunderstorm weather.

91
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:46,000
Over a hundred lives

92
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:46,920
on that plane

93
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:48,040
were in your hands.

94
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:49,040
It was so dangerous.

95
00:06:49,199 --> 00:06:50,920
The moment Hengshi 5123

96
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:51,839
touched down,

97
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:53,040
you became

98
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:54,040
the pride of our whole school.

99
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:56,000
I'm so proud of you.

100
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:58,360
You even remembered the flight number?

101
00:06:59,279 --> 00:06:59,800
Xie Yu,

102
00:07:00,319 --> 00:07:01,439
you're still as amazing as ever.

103
00:07:01,839 --> 00:07:02,519
Photographic memory.

104
00:07:04,399 --> 00:07:05,399
I'm not amazing.

105
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,319
I just care.

106
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:13,199
I...

107
00:07:13,959 --> 00:07:15,160
I mean,

108
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,319
are you pilots

109
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:18,639
usually pretty busy

110
00:07:19,079 --> 00:07:20,120
at work?

111
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:21,439
What do you do after work?

112
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:24,839
Nothing much.

113
00:07:25,519 --> 00:07:27,680
Just eat, hang out,

114
00:07:27,839 --> 00:07:28,759
then go home and sleep.

115
00:07:29,439 --> 00:07:30,279
I thought

116
00:07:30,439 --> 00:07:31,800
you guys had a wide social circle.

117
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:32,360
Must have to

118
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:33,519
deal with all kinds of people.

119
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:34,879
Not really.

120
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:36,800
Our social circle is pretty small.

121
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:38,839
You're a university professor.

122
00:07:39,199 --> 00:07:40,600
We're probably about the same.

123
00:07:42,639 --> 00:07:43,399
Well,

124
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:48,319
are you in a relationship now?

125
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:55,480
No.

126
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:57,079
So...

127
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:00,240
you're not interested in dating right now?

128
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:03,519
Right now,

129
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:05,439
my only focus is getting back to flying.

130
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:08,519
Nothing else.

131
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:16,560
Sixian.

132
00:08:17,879 --> 00:08:18,680
I've really been

133
00:08:19,079 --> 00:08:20,279
following you closely all these years.

134
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,079
And I regret

135
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:24,759
missing out on someone

136
00:08:24,759 --> 00:08:26,279
as great as you back in school.

137
00:08:28,319 --> 00:08:29,360
I keep wondering

138
00:08:29,759 --> 00:08:31,759
whether someone as outstanding, confident,

139
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:33,159
and independent as you

140
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:34,840
also

141
00:08:36,159 --> 00:08:37,960
needs someone by their side

142
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:39,879
to take care of them,

143
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:41,759
lean on,

144
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:44,039
and have their back.

145
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:47,679
I... I may not

146
00:08:47,679 --> 00:08:48,799
be anything special,

147
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:50,039
but I figure

148
00:08:50,159 --> 00:08:50,720
at least

149
00:08:52,879 --> 00:08:54,519
I can get you medicine

150
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:55,799
when you're sick,

151
00:08:58,759 --> 00:09:00,480
bring you cake

152
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:02,000
on your birthday,

153
00:09:04,559 --> 00:09:06,039
and protect you no matter what

154
00:09:06,679 --> 00:09:08,039
when you're in danger.

155
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:23,200
I don't know

156
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:25,960
if you'd be willing to

157
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:26,799
give me a chance.

158
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:34,799
Xie Yu.

159
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:37,960
I really appreciate it.

160
00:09:38,679 --> 00:09:39,759
But

161
00:09:41,639 --> 00:09:42,559
there's someone I like.

162
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,120
I see.

163
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:57,399
But I don't want to regret it this time.

164
00:09:58,799 --> 00:09:59,360
Is there

165
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:01,559
any chance I could still

166
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:02,600
catch up from behind?

167
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:07,120
To be honest,

168
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,759
I did have a crush

169
00:10:10,519 --> 00:10:11,399
on you

170
00:10:11,919 --> 00:10:12,840
back in college.

171
00:10:13,679 --> 00:10:15,039
But lately,

172
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:17,080
I've been running from some things.

173
00:10:18,519 --> 00:10:19,600
And it's because of

174
00:10:20,399 --> 00:10:21,879
what you just said to me

175
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:24,960
that I'm even more certain

176
00:10:26,799 --> 00:10:27,919
of how much I cherish

177
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:29,879
the person I truly love.

178
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,159
I've figured it out.

179
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:36,840
I can't

180
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:38,840
be without him.

181
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:44,159
I'm sorry, Xie Yu.

182
00:10:46,679 --> 00:10:47,120
Water under the bridge.

183
00:10:47,919 --> 00:10:48,399
Water under the bridge.

184
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:49,639
Let's eat.

185
00:11:00,679 --> 00:11:01,320
That's

186
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:02,639
my story

187
00:11:02,639 --> 00:11:04,080
of becoming a pilot

188
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:05,879
at Hengshi Airlines.

189
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:07,080
Thank you all.

190
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:14,000
Thank you, Ruan, for that wonderful talk.

191
00:11:14,159 --> 00:11:15,200
Now we move to the Q&amp;A session.

192
00:11:15,519 --> 00:11:16,720
If you have any questions,

193
00:11:16,879 --> 00:11:17,759
please raise your hand.

194
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:20,440
Yes, this boy.

195
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:22,600
Ruan,

196
00:11:22,759 --> 00:11:23,759
I have a question.

197
00:11:23,879 --> 00:11:24,759
What did it feel like

198
00:11:24,759 --> 00:11:25,840
the first time

199
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:26,720
you flew solo?

200
00:11:27,519 --> 00:11:29,480
First, let me ask you all something.

201
00:11:30,919 --> 00:11:32,399
Has any of you gotten your driver's license?

202
00:11:35,039 --> 00:11:35,759
Quite a few.

203
00:11:36,399 --> 00:11:37,759
Flying solo for the first time

204
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:39,519
feels a lot like

205
00:11:39,679 --> 00:11:41,519
driving a car for the first time.

206
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:42,480
You get nervous.

207
00:11:43,279 --> 00:11:44,919
But mostly excited.

208
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:46,639
Of course,

209
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:47,960
flying

210
00:11:48,399 --> 00:11:49,480
is up in the sky.

211
00:11:50,159 --> 00:11:51,159
That feeling

212
00:11:51,279 --> 00:11:52,600
might be even more intense.

213
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:54,600
Our first time flying solo

214
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:56,200
is called the first solo.

215
00:11:56,759 --> 00:11:57,720
It's a milestone.

216
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,360
After that,

217
00:11:59,519 --> 00:12:00,639
we student pilots

218
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:01,440
have the ability

219
00:12:01,559 --> 00:12:02,879
to fly an aircraft on our own.

220
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:04,519
Kind of like getting your driver's license.

221
00:12:04,919 --> 00:12:05,639
When it was my turn,

222
00:12:05,639 --> 00:12:07,039
my seniors came over,

223
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:08,480
patted me on the shoulder, and said,

224
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:09,320
"Fly well.

225
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:10,159
You got this.

226
00:12:10,519 --> 00:12:11,480
We'll be waiting for you on the ground."

227
00:12:11,879 --> 00:12:13,120
Such simple words.

228
00:12:13,919 --> 00:12:15,039
But every time I fly,

229
00:12:15,279 --> 00:12:16,519
I think of those words.

230
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:18,080
Flying itself is simple,

231
00:12:18,679 --> 00:12:20,240
but the experience is amazing.

232
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:22,799
The first time soaring alone up there,

233
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:23,919
I was greedy.

234
00:12:24,519 --> 00:12:25,960
It felt like the flight was over too soon.

235
00:12:26,919 --> 00:12:27,559
Like

236
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:29,240
being alone with someone

237
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:30,039
you love.

238
00:12:30,679 --> 00:12:31,200
You never get enough.

239
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:32,840
That's when

240
00:12:33,279 --> 00:12:34,080
I realized

241
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,399
I'd fallen in love with the sky.

242
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:37,679
And after our first solo,

243
00:12:38,120 --> 00:12:39,159
there's a tradition.

244
00:12:40,039 --> 00:12:40,799
Ice water drenching.

245
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:42,720
- Ice water drenching.
- For real?

246
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:46,399
My seniors

247
00:12:46,399 --> 00:12:47,159
didn't go easy on me.

248
00:12:47,759 --> 00:12:48,759
A bucket of ice water

249
00:12:48,759 --> 00:12:50,759
from head to toe. Freezing cold.

250
00:12:51,759 --> 00:12:52,759
So that's what they meant

251
00:12:52,759 --> 00:12:53,720
by waiting for me

252
00:12:54,159 --> 00:12:55,240
on the ground.

253
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:57,639
So

254
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,559
why ice water?

255
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:00,480
Good question.

256
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,440
I asked that too.

257
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:04,080
My seniors told me

258
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:06,000
that after the first solo,

259
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,200
one tends to get a big head.

260
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,200
I mean,

261
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,399
you're up in the sky, right?

262
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:11,960
A bucket of ice water

263
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:13,759
is both a celebration

264
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:15,919
and a reminder

265
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:17,200
to stay

266
00:13:17,519 --> 00:13:18,879
level-headed

267
00:13:19,399 --> 00:13:20,080
and not get carried away.

268
00:13:24,639 --> 00:13:25,679
I hereby announce

269
00:13:26,399 --> 00:13:27,480
that the Flight Quality

270
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,039
Reform Plan

271
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:30,799
is officially approved.

272
00:13:31,279 --> 00:13:32,320
Effective

273
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:33,240
September 30,

274
00:13:34,639 --> 00:13:35,399
2025.

275
00:13:36,879 --> 00:13:37,399
Yes!

276
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:10,519
Got some good news to announce.

277
00:14:10,559 --> 00:14:11,720
Mr. Fu's reform

278
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:13,360
passed!

279
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:22,679
Come on. Forward it now.

280
00:14:22,759 --> 00:14:23,039
Come on.

281
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:26,519
Like, comment, and post.

282
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:28,360
Once the reform plan came out,

283
00:14:28,879 --> 00:14:29,480
it completely ended

284
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:30,519
the twenty-plus-year practice

285
00:14:30,519 --> 00:14:31,559
of penalty-based management.

286
00:14:32,039 --> 00:14:32,519
Replaced it

287
00:14:32,519 --> 00:14:33,519
with a healthy safety environment.

288
00:14:34,159 --> 00:14:35,080
Who wouldn't be excited about that?

289
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:40,240
Mr. Fu's reform passed!

290
00:14:42,639 --> 00:14:43,279
That's great!

291
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:44,480
Wonderful!

292
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,360
Let's give the next chance to a girl.

293
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:55,960
Yes, this girl.

294
00:14:56,799 --> 00:14:57,320
Thank you.

295
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,440
Ruan, I'd like to ask something.

296
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,840
What advantages do women have

297
00:15:00,919 --> 00:15:01,879
in learning to fly?

298
00:15:02,519 --> 00:15:03,840
Women don't have any advantages.

299
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:05,399
And it's not just women.

300
00:15:05,799 --> 00:15:06,840
Men don't either.

301
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:08,320
There might be some

302
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:10,000
personal advantages when learning to fly.

303
00:15:10,799 --> 00:15:12,120
For example, science students

304
00:15:12,519 --> 00:15:13,759
might find the theory classes

305
00:15:13,759 --> 00:15:15,039
a bit easier.

306
00:15:15,799 --> 00:15:17,120
But you can't rely on

307
00:15:17,159 --> 00:15:18,559
personal advantages to learn to fly.

308
00:15:19,039 --> 00:15:19,879
We all have to set aside

309
00:15:19,879 --> 00:15:21,639
our pride,

310
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,960
stay grounded, and learn with humility.

311
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:25,039
Because

312
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:26,799
